{
  "title": "Silicon Modulator Exceeding 110 GHz",
  "authors": [
    "Hengsong Yue",
    "Jianbin Fu",
    "Hengwei Zhang",
    "Bo Xiong",
    "Shilong Pan",
    "Tao Chu"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2401.12345",
  "abstract": "This study demonstrates a silicon modulator that exceeds 110 GHz without using resonant structures, achieving on\u2013off keying modulation at 140 Gbaud without digital signal processing. This breakthrough enables silicon modulators to compete with modulators made of thin-film lithium niobate, opening up possibilities for high-speed data transmission applications.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The researchers developed a silicon modulator that uses a <strong>tunable time-frequency equalization technique</strong> to achieve high bandwidth. This technique allows the modulator to operate at high speeds without the need for resonant structures, which can limit the optical bandwidth.",
