    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The modulator uses a <strong>series push-pull configuration</strong> with two PN junctions connected in series. The modulator's response is enhanced by the <strong>tunable time-frequency equalization technique</strong>, which accounts for the relative delay and frequency response in different sections of the modulator.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "A flow diagram illustrating the signal flow through the modulator, showing how the tunable time-frequency equalization technique affects the signal.",
