    {
      "title": "Why It Matters",
      "content": "The development of high-bandwidth silicon modulators is crucial for high-speed data transmission applications. The <strong>elimination of resonant structures</strong> in the design preserves the broad optical bandwidth of the Mach-Zehnder interferometer, making it an efficient solution for parallel data transmission.",
